WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.760
Let's kick off things with some food news.

2
00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:03.960
Okay, too late.

3
00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:07.960
All we do is talk about food.

4
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:08.908
It's true by the way.

5
00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:12.350
Well, they just held the annual CES,

6
00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:15.110
which is the Consumer Electronic Show

7
00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.750
and brands show off all their latest high tech products.

8
00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:21.190
This is like Disneyland for gadgets.

9
00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:22.023
Uh huh.

10
00:00:22.023 --> 00:00:24.550
And I saw something Ross and I had to show you.

11
00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:26.620
Okay, cause I want it real bad.

12
00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:27.960
It's an ice cream robot.

13
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:28.820
No!

14
00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:32.130
Yes, CNET reports, that ColdSnap

15
00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.500
is gonna make a soft serve on demand.

16
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:38.600
Basically, Keurig coffee pods, but with ice cream.

17
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:39.810
2020 was a hard year,

18
00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:42.970
2021 coming through with an ice cream robot.

19
00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:44.060
Thank you so much.

20
00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:45.100 line:15%
I love soft serve.

21
00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.900 line:15%
I used to work at McDonald's

22
00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:49.010 line:15%
and I would do a register, drive-through,

23
00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:50.770 line:15%
and grill the triple threat.

24
00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:53.730 line:15%
And I would do the soft serve cone thing

25
00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:54.760
and I can do the whole thing

26
00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:56.420
with a little (tongue click) at the top.

27
00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:58.920
Like the little like, like.

28
00:00:58.920 --> 00:00:59.890
Perfect little hook.

29
00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:02.590
All I know is McDonald's you're a miracle,

30
00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:03.680
everybody knows it.

31
00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.230
But that ice cream you make

32
00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:06.610
is my favorite ice cream in the world

33
00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:08.820
with the hot fudge and some nuts, oh my God.

34
00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:11.520
Uh huh, I know the half and half, the swirl.

35
00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:13.870
Anyone else in the mood for some sweets right now?

36
00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:15.433
Yes!

37
00:01:15.433 --> 00:01:17.961
Well here's some good news, it's Girl Scout cookie season.

38
00:01:17.961 --> 00:01:19.410
(crowd cheers)

39
00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:21.860
I know, just when you thought you wanted soft serve,

40
00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:23.720
JK, I want Girl Scout cookies.

41
00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:25.510
Food and Wine reports that the girl Scouts

42
00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:28.400
moved their entire operation online.

43
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.050
Remember they used to sit outside the store.

44
00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:30.883
Of course.

45
00:01:30.883 --> 00:01:31.716
I know, I'd always feel bad

46
00:01:31.716 --> 00:01:33.230
cause I'd never buy any.

47
00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:34.680
I'm always on a diet.

48
00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.255
Well, you can order on their website now

49
00:01:36.255 --> 00:01:38.260
through their partnership with Grub Hub.

50
00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:40.620
Okay, and welcome to the future, so easy.

51
00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:42.210
Plus, they've got a brand new cookie

52
00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:46.752
inspired by french toast called Toast Yay.

53
00:01:46.752 --> 00:01:48.180
I like the thin mints.

54
00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:49.470
Do you do those ones?

55
00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:52.060 line:15%
I like the thin mints and to put them in the freezer.

56
00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:52.893 line:15%
I'm that guy.

57
00:01:52.893 --> 00:01:54.260 line:15%
Yeah, I eat so many of them,

58
00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:55.585 line:15%
I call them double chin mints.

59
00:01:55.585 --> 00:01:57.720 line:15%
(crowd laughs)

60
00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.900 line:15%
First of all, why only now?

61
00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:01.270 line:15%
This should have been happening

62
00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:04.270 line:15%
since like the birth of www.HelpMeGetMeSomeGirlScoutCookies.

63
00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:07.150 line:15%
I know it's so much smarter,

64
00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:08.470
you can just order them online.

65
00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:09.660
I do buy them though,

66
00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:12.950
when I see them on the streets, I do.

67
00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:15.720
I always pony up and then.

68
00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:16.920
Yeah, I always have a conversation.

69
00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.680 line:15%
I go, I'd love to support you, but do you see my body?

70
00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:22.540 line:15%
This doesn't happen if I'm eating cookies, sorry.

71
00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:26.320 line:15%
Well, another thing that I really love doing Ross,

72
00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:28.770
is puzzles, big puzzler.

73
00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:29.840
Uh huh, I just started.

74
00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.020
I told you I did my first one in quarantine.

75
00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:34.510
It gave me such anxiety, but now I'm obsessed with them.

76
00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:37.450
I won't do a puzzle if the box is opened.

77
00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:38.283
Why?

78
00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:39.710
Because if I do all that work

79
00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:42.340
and then there's like a missing piece at the end

80
00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:44.417
it's going to send me into an insane asylum.

81
00:02:44.417 --> 00:02:45.740
(Ross laughs)

82
00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:47.270
I'm so close to being there already.

83
00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:49.020
I shan't get that one piece,

84
00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:50.780
to send me to over the edge.

85
00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:52.850
But they're so fun and they are so satisfying.

86
00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:54.700
You can get that last piece in there.

87
00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:58.210
Well, it's great to do alone or with other people.

88
00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:00.810
It's like, it's perfect game.

89
00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:03.070
You know, whether you're alone or with friends.

90
00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:04.520
And I'm so happy

91
00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:07.750
that people are puzzling more than ever right now.

92
00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:10.380
And despite the renewed puzzle passion

93
00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:14.022
there are still some pieces missing in the puzzle industry.

94
00:03:14.022 --> 00:03:14.910
Mm hmm.

95
00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:18.510
And that's where Puzzles Of Color comes in.

96
00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:20.090
It's a small business started

97
00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:23.280
by a brother and a sister duet, from Allen, Texas,

98
00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:26.830
who wanted to bring better representation to puzzles.

99
00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:28.100
And guess what?

100
00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:28.990
What?

101
00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:30.267
They're here!
No.

102
00:03:30.267 --> 00:03:31.950
(crowd cheers)

103
00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:35.774
Please welcome, William Jones and Erica Chambers!

104
00:03:35.774 --> 00:03:36.671
Hi guys!

105
00:03:36.671 --> 00:03:37.588
Hey.
Hi!

106
00:03:38.491 --> 00:03:39.324
Hi.

107
00:03:39.324 --> 00:03:40.801
Oh my gosh, hi.

108
00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:44.409
Our missing puzzle pieces, right here.

109
00:03:44.409 --> 00:03:46.740
Yeah thank you.
Hi.

110
00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:50.340
Erica and William, I love your puzzles.

111
00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:51.730
I love what they stand for.

112
00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.380
I love how they look.

113
00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:57.000
What inspired you to get on and do this?

114
00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.653
It's hard to build a business.

115
00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:02.720 line:15%
We actually grew up doing puzzles as really young kids.

116
00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:05.670 line:15%
We started doing them in elementary school

117
00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:07.200 line:15%
as a winter break thing.

118
00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.600
My mom wanted to keep our minds fresh.

119
00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.730
She wanted to make sure that, you know,

120
00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:13.680
we were entertained during

121
00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:17.220
that week and a half off in between the New Year.

122
00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:19.940
And so as we, you know

123
00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:21.550
we're older and we were trying to find more and more

124
00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:22.383
challenging puzzles.

125
00:04:22.383 --> 00:04:24.350
We realized that we really weren't seeing anything

126
00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:26.590
that featured people of color.

127
00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:27.820
And that was, you know

128
00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:29.500
there wasn't a lot of diversity in the industry.

129
00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:32.920
So we decided we'd try to see if we could change that.

130
00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:34.360
That's so cool, I love that,

131
00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:35.680
that there's such a purpose behind it.

132
00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:36.920
I also love that footage too.

133
00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:38.560
Watching how they cut the puzzles.

134
00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:40.240
I didn't know that's how you did it.

135
00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:41.073
That's do neat!

136
00:04:41.073 --> 00:04:42.930
I also wonder how you pick your images.

137
00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:44.120
See there we're looking at the footage

138
00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:44.953
of how they cut it.

139
00:04:44.953 --> 00:04:45.786
Yup.

140
00:04:45.786 --> 00:04:47.270
And so the puzzles flipped upside down

141
00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:49.150
and when you flip it up, you can see how beautiful.

142
00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:50.580
How do you pick the pictures,

143
00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:52.150
like that one right there?

144
00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:53.615
Who makes that, does the art?

145
00:04:53.615 --> 00:04:56.026
We find artists of color.

146
00:04:56.026 --> 00:04:57.007
More likely social media

147
00:04:57.007 --> 00:04:59.430
and like, really like talking to the artists,

148
00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:00.360
getting their backstory

149
00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:02.440
and getting the story behind the actual puzzle itself.

150
00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:03.570
To really like, you know,

151
00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.610
we want to make sure we're telling a diverse story.

152
00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:08.530
Or telling a story of anybody can relate to or anything.

153
00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:10.460
Anybody who sees this would be like,

154
00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:11.293
yeah, that's great a great puzzle.

155
00:05:11.293 --> 00:05:13.220
I need to have that in my house as art.

156
00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:14.290
That's great, and you have done,

157
00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:17.950
you've done like eight puzzles all out of Erica's garage.

158
00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:18.783
What's next?

159
00:05:18.783 --> 00:05:19.616
Yeah, so far.

160
00:05:19.616 --> 00:05:21.140
Then you're taking over the world.

161
00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:23.040
So what do you do next with the business?

162
00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:24.860
We really love our artists

163
00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:26.600
and so we're trying to highlight them

164
00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:27.600
in the best way possible.

165
00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:31.230
So we're doing a little video series with our artists

166
00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.800
and of course always looking for more and more art.

167
00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:36.460
Well, we'd love to feature you on the website

168
00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:38.840 line:15%
and continue to talk about you guys

169
00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:41.430 line:15%
and shine a light on the important

170
00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:43.720 line:15%
and beautiful thing you are doing

171
00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:45.980
and hearing as a parent that your mom

172
00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:48.560
encouraged you to do puzzles growing up.

173
00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:51.800
Like I'm the bigger puzzler and I don't have my kids do it.

174
00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:54.340
And I feel like I've learned a lesson today,

175
00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:56.460
that I need to get my kids involved more.

176
00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:59.740
Yeah, absolutely, it's a great time to bond.

177
00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:02.040
Like that's how we are, you know, we're really, really close

178
00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.810
because I think a lot, and in part,

179
00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:06.640
because of doing puzzles together for so many years.

180
00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:08.450
I'm worried I'd take them too seriously

181
00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:10.167
to let my children get involved.

182
00:06:10.167 --> 00:06:11.630
Me too.
I could see that.

183
00:06:11.630 --> 00:06:12.463
Yeah.

184
00:06:12.463 --> 00:06:14.260
We definitely, we did have a situation

185
00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:16.330
when we were younger where one of our cousins

186
00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:17.163
was helping and lost some puzzle pieces.

187
00:06:17.163 --> 00:06:18.816
Oh my gosh.
Oh no.

188
00:06:18.816 --> 00:06:20.630
And it was, it was disaster.

189
00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:23.740
Yeah, well, I'm that guy.

190
00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:26.250
Who's like, you take it seriously.

191
00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:30.600
So go to our website at the DrewBarrymoreShow.com

192
00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:32.580 line:15%
where we're going to feature all these puzzles,

193
00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:34.510 line:15%
how to send an art, where to buy it.

194
00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:36.950 line:15%
Erica and William, thank you so much,

195
00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.060
for being on our show

196
00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:40.970
and help illuminating this gorgeous business

197
00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:43.500
of PuzzlesOfColor.com.

198
00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:45.844 line:15%
And thank you for being on the show today.

199
00:06:45.844 --> 00:06:48.427 line:15%
(upbeat music)

